extraction_notes: "THE POWER LISTS ARE NAMED RATHER THAN GATED BY CATEGORY, which is how survey G8''s taxonomy mismatch stops mattering. This book files a psi-power as Major or Secondary and the catalog files one as Healing, Physical, Sensitive or Super; the two do not map, and `powers_from` on a starting group REPLACES the category gate outright. `psionics.type` is `master` for the same reason: nothing here gates on tier, and a lower tier would have filtered the Super rows out of a list the book says this character may take. Thirty-three names, all resolved against production - three of them under a catalog spelling this book does not use (`Bio-Manipulation (the evil eye)`, `Empathic Transmission`, `Object Read (Psychometry)`), and four created by `add-hu-core-psionics.sql`. THE +10 I.S.P. PER LEVEL IS IN `level_progression` AND NOT IN A FORMULA: `isp_base` is rolled once at creation and nothing re-evaluates it, so a per-level gain has no field. It is stated on every level rather than once, because the book''s own sentence - ''this 10 I.S.P. starts at level one, so even a new character gets the extra 10'' - is easy to read as a level-2 gain and is not. PSIONIC ATTACKS PER MELEE have no field either; `combat.attacks` is the hand-to-hand number, and the book keeps the two apart on purpose - a psionic attack does not consume a physical one. Recorded per level for the same reason."
---

## Lore

Psionics, or Extra Sensory Perception, are paranormal powers of the mind:
telepathy, empathy, telekinesis and so on. It is believed that all or most
humans have some degree of psionic ability, but most ordinary people exhibit
little or none. An average person may occasionally get a feeling about something
or sense a loved one in need, and that is hardly a world-stomping power.

Psionics as a SUPER ability means something else: exceptional, super-developed
mind powers. Powers that can stop a car or read minds.

Three power categories may hold mind powers - Mutants, Aliens and Psionics - and
in the first two the player rolls to see whether his character has any. Those
who fall into the psionic category on the random power table are **natural
psionics**: humans, not mutants, who exhibit incredibly developed mind powers.
The natural psionic is the most powerful of all psionic individuals, with the
greatest variety and number of mental powers, and a mutant or alien psychic is
somewhat more limited - two major and four secondary powers against this
character''s three and six.

Even ordinary people have a chance of fighting off a psionic attack; those with
psionic ability have a much better defence. A 20-sided die is rolled to mentally
parry, and a high roll means the person is simply not affected. Some powers have
no saving throw at all - telekinesis, levitation, pyrokinesis, presence sense
and mind bolt among them.

## GM Notes

**Inner Strength Points** are the person''s inner mental strength, and each power
states what it costs. When the I.S.P. is gone the psionic can do nothing more
until he rests. Recovery is 2 I.S.P. per hour of total relaxation or sleep, or
**4 per hour through meditation**, which is an automatic ability for a psionic
rather than a skill to be learned.

**Psionic attacks per melee** are counted apart from hand to hand attacks: two
at level one, one more at levels three, five, seven, nine and twelve. Hand to
hand combat skills are not automatic and must be selected as learned skills;
every hero gets two physical attacks per melee regardless.

Unless the character is extremely wealthy, only conventional weaponry and body
armour are available. Any alignment may be chosen, though heroes should
generally be of good alignment.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-psionics');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-psionics';

